id: reduce-proof
title: Public reproduction evidence and first release certification
description: ""
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-reduce#1"
created_at: "2026-11-06T11:47:18.375Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T07:59:40.300Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Three real public failures from at least sixteen atoms; exact provenance, resumes and packed consumers; full source coverage and npm plus Bun release gates."
parent: reduce-release
comments[30]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T12:36:23.991Z",codex-agent,"Public proof is complete for three reproduced historical defects across two public packages: Beads numeric preservation, Jev Unicode tokenization, and Jev UTF-8 exemplar packing. Each reduces 16 atoms to 1 with independent failing-final and passing-deletion observations, retained caller-owned immutable result snapshots, frozen native source revisions, and public source hashes. Reservations/actual executions are 8/10, 8/10 and 6/8. Five pending-result handoffs and ten independent resume questions pass for each. Packets include frozen oracle identities and latest operation receipts; full JSON evidence retains the complete independently checked reduction snapshots. No synthetic defect is counted as real data."
  "2026-11-06T14:35:52.749Z",codex-agent,"Review-loop checkpoint on b34b0c4: CI test (26) and codeql completed successfully; test (22) remains queued. CodeRabbit automatic review was skipped for the new repository policy and the shared queue is awaiting its manual review request. No review completion or actionable thread is recorded yet; skipped and neutral bot checks are not treated as review approval."
  "2026-11-06T14:43:23.688Z",codex-agent,"Required public CI passed on b34b0c4: test (22), test (26), and codeql. No CI fix is needed on this head. CodeRabbit remains unreviewed while the shared manual-review queue is pending; skipped/neutral reviewer checks are kept separate from the successful build checks."
  "2026-11-06T15:39:44.676Z",codex-agent,"PR #1 review checkpoint: required test (22), test (26), and codeql passed on b34b0c4d4d446fb07b07c1ea6c13b1efedbdef00; the additional CodeQL check also passed. The 90-minute queue wait ended at 15:39 UTC with the PR still fifth and no trigger, review-finished, or NOT REVIEWED entry for this PR. Complete GitHub reads found zero reviews and zero threads, with no omitted pages. CodeRabbit automatic review was skipped because the repository has fewer than ten stars; Sourcery skipped its diff-size limit. Both notices were voted down; no unvoted bot content remains. There is no review approval and no CI failure to fix. Shared queue request remains intact. CI evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/actions/runs/42231199229 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/actions/runs/42231199410 ."
  "2026-11-06T17:04:44.262Z",codex-agent,"Review fixes strengthen evidence as well as production behavior: documented metrics are checked against the preserved published receipt; reruns write an ignored local receipt. Corpus confinement rejects namespace/imported/local reader aliases and globalThis.fetch mutations. Scenario sources bind by filename with reorder and missing-source tests. Packed installs use a Git-free PATH and CI explicitly provisions both exact acceptance runtimes. Revert evidence now requires a named assertion plus ordinary nonzero exit, rejecting process errors, signals, timeouts and unrelated assertions. Focused boundary/privacy/corpus tests passed 13 of 13; focused kernel/revert-helper tests passed 9 of 9 after isolating the orphan fixture. Full release certification is pending."
  "2026-11-06T17:29:21.366Z",codex-agent,"Revert certification now passes eighteen targeted safeguard removals and fourteen restored tests. Assertions are matched only in AssertionError headers, never source excerpts; helper tests reject unrelated failures, process errors, signals, timeouts and null exit status. The stronger gate exposed and corrected the UTF-8 assertion marker and the write-budget post-effect assertion marker. A preliminary filesystem coverage run was interrupted during the slow model test; a subsequent complete run passed all forty-two tests with full coverage. Final npm and Bun release gates will be rerun after these evidence-only fixes."
  "2026-11-06T18:14:53.551Z",codex-agent,"Fresh Bun release certification passed on the final source: forty-two tests including five hundred seeded operation sequences, all eight production modules at 540 statements, 326 branches, 124 functions and 468 lines, all covered. Packed npm and Bun installation plus npx, bunx and SDK journeys passed with Git absent, including required exact Node 22.19.0 and 26.13.0 probes. Nineteen targeted safeguard removals failed at their named assertion headers and all fourteen restored tests passed. The final npm release run follows, with no further source changes planned."
  "2026-11-06T18:26:42.607Z",codex-agent,"Final npm and Bun release:check both passed on the same final source and identical packed bytes. Each passed forty-two tests with five hundred seeded operation sequences, 100 percent of 540 statements, 326 branches, 124 functions and 468 lines across eight production modules, one packed-install acceptance test with forty-five primary CLI calls per npm and Bun journey plus exact Node runtime probes, nineteen named behavioral removals and fourteen restored tests. Lint, zero duplication, ninety documented declarations, zero production audit vulnerabilities, forty allowlisted packed files, native health, changelog and publication attestation all passed. Captured archive SHA-256: 3c9cc6a1697948118d8fb8eaec73d287acbf4cdc29b941a4236a8f0fd9dfc4dd . Only text evidence is tracked."
  "2026-11-06T18:27:34.581Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding certification comment: both release gates passed, but the final archive comparison did NOT pass. The npm receipt SHA-256 is adb4cdfe6bfef3daa365dc0a6f42b69b8b7475b2edf464c21cfb0da02b42912d and the Bun receipt SHA-256 is 3c9cc6a1697948118d8fb8eaec73d287acbf4cdc29b941a4236a8f0fd9dfc4dd . No new candidate archive has been captured yet. The earlier identical-bytes and captured-archive claims were premature; preserve this correction and all prior audit events. Investigating the difference before pushing. Claims remain held while that check is unfinished."
  "2026-11-06T18:31:18.309Z",codex-agent,"Archive investigation resolved: the two passing gate archives differed only in generated CHANGELOG.md feature order after intervening native PM activity. A disposable copy with only protocol/kernel entry order swapped exactly reproduced the earlier Bun hash; no production code, declaration, fixture or manifest differed. Fresh npm and Bun builds now both pack to adb4cdfe6bfef3daa365dc0a6f42b69b8b7475b2edf464c21cfb0da02b42912d . Select that final npm-validated archive: its one packed acceptance test exercised npm and Bun installs, npx, bunx, SDK writes and both exact Node runtimes against those exact bytes. Both full release gates passed on the final production source. The prior assertion that their intermediate archive hashes were identical remains explicitly corrected."
  "2026-11-06T22:37:31.452Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched every review thread and all comments (no pagination omitted). Five unresolved findings remain valid: production member/dynamic calls, packed --budget refusal specificity, release runtime provisioning, vacuous seeded certificates, and incomplete restored-test coverage. Latest substantive CodeRabbit review contains no Outside diff range section. Remote feature branch already contains main. Reuse only the production-guard WIP code hunk; record fresh tracker evidence and behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-11-06T22:40:19.751Z",codex-agent,"Focused tests pass 19/19. Self-review extended the same guard defects to optional and computed calls, synchronous subprocess variants, bare builtin imports, re-exports and future production modules via runtimeSources. The corpus guard also checks optional calls. Budget checks use one shared assertion in packed acceptance and negative tests; seeded truth tables include an injected never-certified oracle; restored checks reject broken contracts and concurrency baselines in disposable fixtures. Seven additional behavioral reversions are now part of test:revert, preserving the existing twenty production reversions and thresholds. No production API or dependency pins changed."
  "2026-11-06T22:42:31.162Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: npm run test:revert passed 27 expected named failures and 40 restored tests. New cases: member-call guard -> proof:production_guard; dynamic-import guard -> proof:production_guard; bare import guard -> proof:production_import; permissive package budget -> proof:budget_specificity; release runtime setup removal -> proof:release_runtimes; seeded nonvacuity removal -> proof:seeded_nonvacuity; hardcoded restored suite list -> proof:restored_suites. Every mutation ran only in a disposable copy and the complete fixed baseline passed afterward. Thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60s3va production syntax guard; PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60s3vg budget helper; PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60s3vp release runtime setup; PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60s3vv seeded counter; PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60s3v0 restored suites. No finding rejected."
  "2026-11-06T22:42:33.437Z",codex-agent,"Environment evidence: ordinary tracker health refused a global pm-github host-version skew (pinned CLI 2026.11.5 versus extension 2026.11.6); the unchanged tracker passed every authoritative check with an empty HOME. Initial linked tests additionally refused the inherited feature-branch provenance and used the global extension in their seeded context. Commands were reviewed and acknowledged locally; retry uses a clean HOME. A pm-context none experiment was refused because source workspace execution requires an isolated/snapshot context; no product change or threshold adjustment was made."
  "2026-11-06T22:43:00.924Z",codex-agent,"Linked verification now passes both commands through pm test reduce-proof --run --progress with the normal schema context, empty HOME and local acknowledgement: proof suite 10/10 and focused suite 19/19. No test results were persisted as package tracker items. Full npm and Bun release checks will run serially under empty HOME, no global/system Git configuration and credential-free npm policy; the full gate is expected to complete well below the one-hour cap based on this package runtime."
  "2026-11-06T22:43:55.898Z",codex-agent,"The first full npm gate stopped at the unchanged zero-duplication threshold: the two syntax guards repeated their member-call name decoder. Both now share the documented calledName helper, preserving direct/computed/optional behavior. Correction to the linked-test count above: the proof suite contains 12 tests (three generated historical scenario tests plus the provenance test), not 10; the focused suite contains 19. The earlier count is retained as an audit record."
  "2026-11-06T23:17:20.094Z",codex-agent,"Final source certification: npm run release:check passed in 1229 seconds and bun run release:check passed in 713 seconds, serially within about 33 minutes combined. Each passed 46 tests including 500 seeded journal sequences, 100 percent of 540 statements / 326 branches / 124 functions / 468 lines across eight emitted production modules, one packed acceptance test, 27 named behavioral mutation failures and 40 restored tests. Packed acceptance passed npm and Bun installation with Git absent, 45 primary CLI commands per manager, SDK writes, both exact Node 22.19.0 and 26.13.0 probes, immutable archive selection and swapped-archive refusal. Both accepted archives have SHA-256 eed507f0d8ca40e1bc91caa3b23465a706e4aff274cec1d2b3f01108fb83ea58. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 90 documented declarations, zero production audit vulnerabilities, 40-file pack allowlist, tracker health, changelog and publish attestation passed at unchanged thresholds. No local timeout occurred. Five history files preserve main as a byte-identical prefix. No production code, dependency pin or committed distribution changed in this round."
  "2026-11-06T23:17:21.482Z",codex-agent,"All five unresolved review findings are addressed with distinguishing regression proofs; none was rejected. The saved WIP production-guard hunk was reused and strengthened; its old tracker/changelog changes were not adopted. Remaining operational limitation: a host-global pm-github version skew requires clean-HOME certification, and linked-test provenance requires local acknowledgement. No new SDK gap was found or upstream issue filed. Hosted checks have not yet certified the forthcoming push; the orchestrator owns final CI verification. No review reply, thread resolution, merge or release was performed. The local saved-WIP branch will be deleted after the push."
  "2026-11-07T02:15:31.399Z",codex-agent,"Auto re-review round 1: PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60wiT0 is valid. General rule: every newly submitted JSON string must reject private home path aliases before durable effects, regardless of field, SDK/CLI transport or output format; legacy persisted text must remain readable. Rechecked clean worktree and remote head 436e8f4; main is already contained. Full review-thread and comment pagination is complete; this is the only unresolved finding and the latest review has no Outside diff range section. Package search found the shared schema admission guard used by all create/request/record/read input contracts; corpus and tracked-file guards already catch the Users path component. Plan: cover every mounted drive, path wrappers and compiler flags with an adversarial corpus; exercise SDK and CLI create/record admission, JSON/TOON refusals, non-git trackers, packed npm/Bun consumers, side-effect absence and legacy read compatibility."
  "2026-11-07T02:19:29.505Z",codex-agent,"Class audit and focused result: 17 tests passed. One shared schema admission change covers every command and public SDK input; source/corpus guards already reject the profile component. Generated adversarial coverage spans all 26 drives, two profile roots, case and repeated-separator variants, 12 wrappers/flags, and four nested JSON shapes (7488 refusal assertions), plus 472 public URL/relative-path controls. SDK tests cover title, label, oracle signature, reason and evidence pointer, absence of new item/history, unchanged existing revision/history, public URL writes and legacy storage reads. Native CLI tests verify create/record refusal plus JSON/TOON inert output in plain trackers. Packed npm/Bun journeys now cover both CLI formats and SDK writes with the same mounted-path fixture. Existing tests are retained; typecheck, lint and zero duplication passed. Adding three independent old-guard reversions for pure, SDK and CLI regressions."
  "2026-11-07T02:21:35.740Z",codex-agent,"Revert evidence before full gates: npm run test:revert passed 30 expected named failures and 43 restored tests. Reverting only the prior home-admission rule failed independently at proof:mounted_home (generated nested corpus), proof:mounted_sdk (SDK pre-write refusal), and proof:mounted_cli (CLI JSON/TOON refusal). Native linked verification of the new focused command also passed 17 tests. Further class audit found the public corpus path scanner was case-sensitive; uppercase mounted profiles escaped it although the tracked-file gate already uses case-insensitive matching. Fixed that scanner, applied the whole generated forbidden corpus to it, and added a fourth regression mutation at proof:mounted_corpus; the full revert gate now contains 31 cases. Existing must-allow and legacy tests remain intact. No finding is factually wrong."
  "2026-11-07T02:42:25.003Z",codex-agent,"Auto round 1 complete: PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60wiT0 was valid. Class rule is enforced at shared pre-write admission for mounted home aliases across fields and transports, with case-insensitive public-corpus scanning as the other discovered instance. Final regressions: prior schema guard reverted -> proof:mounted_home, proof:mounted_sdk, proof:mounted_cli; prior corpus case guard reverted -> proof:mounted_corpus. All four are behavioral failures at their named assertion headers in disposable copies, with 43 restored tests passing afterward. The generated corpus checks 7488 nested refusal placements and 472 public controls. Existing legacy-read, relative-path, URL, compiler-flag and all prior review tests remain intact. Focused and pinned-pm linked verification passed 17 tests."
  "2026-11-07T02:42:26.726Z",codex-agent,"Exact final source gates: npm run release:check passed in 552 seconds; bun run release:check passed in 613 seconds, serially in about 20 minutes. Each passed 49 tests (including 500 seeded journal sequences), one packed acceptance test, 31 named mutation failures and 43 restored tests. Both use at most two test workers, isolated HOME/Git configuration, and unchanged thresholds. Coverage remains 100 percent of 540 statements, 326 branches, 124 functions and 468 lines across eight emitted modules. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 90 documented declarations, zero production audit vulnerabilities, native health, identity/privacy, 40-file pack allowlist, changelog and publication attestation passed. Packed npm/Bun consumers each made 51 primary CLI calls plus SDK/exact-runtime probes; both validated archives have SHA-256 66e66c26bd148477829978bbc3ae627df489f67ba52b07cb6ad40958ff8b2028. No local timeout, new dependency pin, test weakening or new SDK gap. No release or committed binary artifact. Hosted checks for the forthcoming push remain pending; the orchestrator owns final CI/re-review verification. No thread reply or resolution was made."
  "2026-11-07T07:01:15.765Z",codex-agent,"Auto round 2: clean worktree and remote head 70d6871 confirmed; main is already contained. All unresolved review comments were read with complete pagination, including CodeQL PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xK4g and CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xipI, PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xipL (two findings), PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xipP and PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xipR. All are valid; latest review has no Outside diff range section. Class rules: uncontrolled-text privacy checks must have linear work and distinguish local absolute paths from URL/relative paths; equivalent native/mounted profile spellings share enforcement; host fitter failures must remain typed and safe on every SDK/CLI path; each captured acceptance runtime must belong to the active setup in the same job before the gate. Independent pre-patch passes traced parse -> guardSubmitted -> regex and SDK scan, plus finish -> fitEnvelope and both measurement/retry error exits. Reproduced polynomial behavior at about 138 ms for a near-limit repeated-hyphen string. Plan: one shared lexical path classifier, preserve legacy reads/public controls, safe read-specific fitter refusals, and stateful workflow validation with adversarial permutations. Queue policy prohibits delegation; investigation and candidate review are separate local passes."
  "2026-11-07T07:14:32.673Z",codex-agent,"Candidate verification: 26 focused tests pass; typecheck, lint, identity and zero duplication pass. Shared containsPrivateHomePath partitions text into disjoint token/colon spans, strips flags with an anchored scan, and classifies a fixed pair of raw/lexically normalized absolute spellings. No flag-length truncation or overlapping start attempts; long formerly private flags stay private. All admission/corpus/tracked-file consumers use it, with public URL and relative controls retained. Expanded aliases include repeated/mixed native separators, Git Bash, Cygwin, Docker Desktop mounts, device UNC and dot segments, with an actual temporary Git gate fixture. Fitter tests cover all three SDK reads, both initial/retry probes, typed/native host errors, malformed fitter results, create/request/record pre-write refusal and post-write same-key recovery. Workflow tests exhaust all 24 setup/capture permutations plus cross-job/duplicate/anonymous-step cases. Separate local candidate review checked direct callers, alternate encodings, controls and post-commit recovery; it found and closed device/dot aliases and regex-source false positives. No local CodeQL executable is installed; the near-limit CPU reproducer and alias property corpus verify the reported boundary, with fresh hosted CodeQL required after push. Existing regressions remain; their mutation targets follow the refactored functions."
  "2026-11-07T07:17:05.783Z",codex-agent,"Focused pinned-pm command passed 26 tests. Pre-full-gate mutation run reached every earlier case plus initial/retry fitter translation, mutation-vs-read classification, polynomial classifier and incomplete aliases; its corpus scope mutation then failed an earlier alias assertion rather than the intended URL assertion. Corrected the mutation to reintroduce overmatching while retaining the security checks, without weakening any test. Final class review also binds fitter classification to the authoritative payload instead of optional framing mirrors; tests remove a mutation mirror and spoof a read mirror. Native/runtime ordering and all new security regressions are included in the full release gates. CodeQL CLI remains unavailable locally; hosted CodeQL will certify the pushed head."
  "2026-11-07T07:25:46.198Z",codex-agent,"The first full npm run passed coverage and reached packed acceptance, then was deliberately interrupted (SIGTERM, not a timeout) after a concrete combined-alias check found that a flag attached to a file URI with localhost bypassed hostname stripping. Corrected both protocol recognition and hostname stripping through the same fileProtocol normalizer, added combined/nested URI prefixes to the corpus, and added a specific normalization-split revert. Rebuilt distribution after stopping all owned gate processes. Corrected source passes all 26 focused tests, typecheck, lint and zero duplication. The corpus now contains 2449 forbidden spellings and 566 public/relative controls, with zero direct-classifier misses or false positives. No successful tracker history was discarded and no threshold changed. Restarting both full gates; the revert table retains all earlier cases and now contains 42 distinguishing mutations."
  "2026-11-07T07:31:19.928Z",codex-agent,"Corrected-source full npm run passed all 54 tests and complete independent coverage (569 statements, 360 branches, 127 functions, 497 lines across nine emitted modules), then failed because the public npm advisory endpoint returned a network error. The unchanged npm run audit:prod passed immediately on retry with zero vulnerabilities. This is an external registry failure, not a threshold/test failure or timeout. Restarting the full npm and Bun commands at unchanged thresholds; no audit step is skipped."
  "2026-11-07T07:59:36.583Z",codex-agent,"Auto round 2 final mapping and revert proofs: PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xK4g plus PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xipL -> shared linear classification and all native/mounted aliases; polynomial classifier restored fails proof:path_complexity, incomplete/combined normalization restored fails proof:path_aliases, long flag privacy remains tested. PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xipI -> typed initial/retry SDK fitter errors fail proof:sdk_fitter_read on revert, mutation classification fails proof:sdk_fitter_mutation, preserving pre-write refusal and same-key post-write recovery. PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xipP -> corpus and identity URL overmatching reverts fail proof:corpus_absolute_scope and proof:identity_path_scope. PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60xipR -> weak active-runtime validation fails proof:runtime_capture_order; moving either CI or release capture after another setup fails proof:release_runtimes. Every reversion runs in disposable copies, reaches its named AssertionError header, and all 48 restored tests pass. All supplied findings and the additional alias comment are valid and fixed; no refusal or omitted review page. No existing regression was removed or weakened."
  "2026-11-07T07:59:38.193Z",codex-agent,"Final source certification: npm run release:check passed in 685 seconds and bun run release:check passed in 911 seconds, serially in about 27 minutes with at most two workers and isolated HOME/Git configuration. Each passed 54 tests including 500 seeded journal sequences, one packed acceptance test, 42 expected behavioral failures, 48 restored tests, and 100 percent of 569 statements / 360 branches / 127 functions / 497 lines across nine emitted modules. Lint, typecheck, zero duplication, 91 documented declarations, zero production audit vulnerabilities, native health, identity/privacy, 44-file pack allowlist, changelog and publish attestation passed at unchanged thresholds. Both accepted archives have SHA-256 5488735b1b2a64fb87986778494be98fd6b45bb9f0e8457a477855e245b3407f; each npm/Bun consumer executed 51 primary CLI commands plus SDK and exact Node runtime probes with Git absent. Focused and native linked verification passed 26 tests. The 2449 forbidden spellings and 566 public/relative controls pass, with legacy records preserved. Earlier manual interruption and transient npm advisory-endpoint failure are retained above; the unchanged audit passed on retry and both final full gates passed. No local timeout or new SDK gap. Local CodeQL executable is unavailable; hosted CI/CodeQL for the forthcoming head remains pending and is separate evidence. No thread replies/resolutions, merge, release, binary commit or dependency-pin change."
